
Ingestion:
In AI, ingestion (or data ingestion) is the intake phase. It is the very first step where raw, messy real-world data is collected, 
cleaned, structured, and imported into your system so an AI model can actually read and use it.


ingestion_pipeline.py
        │
        │ config
        ▼
     Document
        │
        ├── Loader
        ├── Parser
        ├── Preprocessor
        ├── Chunker
        ├── Embedder
        └── Storer

ML pipeline:
Raw Data Sources  ➡️  Data Wrangling  ➡️  Data Cleaning  ➡️  Feature Engineering  ➡️  Model Ready Data

1. Data Wrangling (The Structuring Phase)
   Data wrangling (sometimes called data munging) focuses on the form and structure of your data. 
   It is the process of gathering data from multiple sources and reshaping it into a workable format.Combining Data: Running joins, 
   merges, or concatenations across different databases or CSV files.Reshaping: Pivoting tables from a "wide" format to a "long" 
   format or aggregation (e.g., grouping hourly temperature data into daily averages).Type Casting: Ensuring columns have the 
   correct data types (e.g., turning a text column containing numbers into actual numeric float types).

   1⃣️ Combining Data: Running joins, merges, or concatenations across different databases or CSV files.
   2⃣️ Reshaping: Pivoting tables from a "wide" format to a "long" format or aggregation (e.g., grouping hourly temperature data 
     into daily averages).
   3⃣️ Type Casting: Ensuring columns have the correct data types (e.g., turning a text column containing numbers into actual 
     numeric float types).

2. Data Cleaning (The Quality Phase)
   Data cleaning focuses on the health and accuracy of the data within that structure. It fixes errors, omissions, and noise.

   1⃣️ Handling Missing Values: Deciding whether to drop rows with missing information or fill them in (imputation) using the mean, 
     median, or a placeholder value.
   2⃣️ Deduplication: Finding and removing identical rows or duplicate records.
   3⃣️ Outlier Removal: Identifying anomalies (like a human age column showing 150 or -5) and correcting or filtering them out.
   4⃣️ Structural Fixes: Fixing typos, standardization (like forcing all country names to be lowercase uppercase codes like US 
     instead of usa or United States), and whitespace normalization.

3. Feature Engineering & Preprocessing (The Math Phase)
   Once the data is clean and structured, it must be converted into numerical values that ML models can ingest.

   1⃣️ Encoding Categorical Data: Turning text classes (like ["Red", "Blue", "Green"]) into numbers using techniques like One-Hot 
     Encoding.
   2⃣️ Scaling & Normalization: Shrinking numeric ranges (e.g., mapping a salary column ranging from $30k–$200k down to a uniform 
     decimal range between 0 and 1) so large numbers don't skew the model's math.

🔄 Direct Comparison: ML vs. RAG Pipeline
   One caveat: not force the correspondence too literally. In ML, feature engineering creates features for the model; 
   in RAG, embeddings are usually created after the document has been parsed/chunked/preprocessed. So they're analogous pipeline 
   stages, not exact equivalents.

   RAG Pipeline           |  ML Pipeline Equivalent    | Why it belongs there
   -----------------------|---------------------|---------------------
   Extracting text        | Data Wrangling      | You are changing the physical structure from
   from a PDF file        |                     | a file format to an accessible raw string
   -----------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------
   Normalizing whitespace | Data Cleaning       | You are deleting formatting errors and
   / stripping tabs       |                     | cleaning up noise in the text.
   -----------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------
   Chunking text into 500~| Data reshaping      | You are slicing the global data array into 
   word blocks            |                     | uniformly structured rows.
   -----------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------
   Generating an embedding| Feature Eng         | You are converting clean human text into
   via a emedding model   |                     | numerical cooridinates (vectors)
   -----------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------


